RF.put("questb:b36",{"8596":{"id":8596,"t":"Footwraps of the Oracle","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of Death, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Gold Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj. This quest also requires Neutral faction with the Brood of Nozdormu.\nQiraji Bindings of Command Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Death Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"Qiraji magic is strong and ancient. The most powerful qiraji wield items of such might, they'd give pause even to a dragon.\nBring me the qiraji bindings of command and other minor components by and I'll create a set of powerful boots for you.\nYou will find them useful in the fight against the enemy.","rew":"You will receive:\nFootwraps of the Oracle\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. You've proven you're no ordinary mortal.\nI give you these with the confidence they'll aid you in crushing the vile qiraji.\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Priest Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8596\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Footwraps of the Oracle this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of Death, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Gold Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8516":{"id":8516,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Thick Leather!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 thick leather to Marta Finespindle at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n10 Thick Leather Razzashi Cobra 37.5 % in Zul'Gurub , Felsteel Chest 7.1 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 4.5 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 4.5 % and 4 more","desc":"Yep, the stack's still not high enough. ‹name›, we still haven't reached our goal of $2071w thick leather. Just think of all the things that we can make with all of that leather! All kinds of armor and weapons. Stuff for inside the steam tanks and rifle scopes! Engineering goggles, and I bet if it ends up that we collect too much we could give the rest to the Horde for their zeppelins!\nYou gonna bring me back some more thick leather?","rew":"You will receive:\n7 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Yep, the stack's still not high enough. ‹name›, we still haven't reached our thick leather goal. Just think of all the things that we can make with all of that leather! All kinds of armor and weapons. Stuff for inside the steam tanks and rifle scopes! And engineering goggles, those are always fun!\nYou gonna bring me back some more thick leather?","done":"You did it again! That is simply amazing how you go out there, collect all of this stuff, and then bring it back here and hand it over. I tell ya, when they find out how much you've been helping out around here you're not going to be able to walk down the street without people asking you for your autograph!\nThanks again for your very generous donation of thick leather, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.6,"y":33.3,"n":"Marta Finespindle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8436":{"id":8436,"t":"Conquering Arathi Basin","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,000 experience instead of 3,300, 0.91 times as much.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Our conflict with the Alliance has escalated to a true war. No longer are false pretenses to enter into battle used or expected by either side at this point.\nThe battle for the Arathi Basin is one of resources, plain and simple. Either the Alliance gets the resources and uses them against us or we get them and use them to keep our war efforts going. Help the Defilers maintain the flow of resources we need, ‹name›!","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,000\n+100 reputation with The Defilers","back":"You've come back with news from Arathi, ‹class›?","done":"Securing our resources in Arathi is an important task! You've done well, ‹name›.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8996":{"id":8996,"t":"Return to Bodley","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain and give him the Brazier of Beckoning.\nBrazier of Beckoning","desc":"I will ignore your impertinence this time, ‹class›, because you have done a noble thing today; returning the rest of my stolen spirit to me. Despite your obviously weak nature, ‹race›, you have shown courage where those that stole from me did not, and probably never could!\nReturn to them, before I change my mind and slay you where you stand. Go back and tell them that they are safe... for now.","rew":"You will receive:\nBrazier of Invocation Brazier of Invocation: User's Manual\nExperience: 650","back":"‹name›, you're back and still alive! Well, at least that makes one of us.\nYou're going to have to tell me all about it!","done":"He really said all of that? Wow, I can't believe he's going to call off the spectral assassins and stalkers, even if he did hint at causing my living companions further harm in the future.\nThis is a great day, ‹name›! You've accomplished what few ever could, and absolved us, at least in part, of some of our past sins.\nThank you! As a sign of appreciation, I'd like to give you this. You can use it to summon forth spirits at the same haunted locations that you already have, and a few others, too.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"2756":{"id":2756,"t":"The Old Ways","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring four Steel Breastplates and four Steel Plate Helms to Aturk the Anvil in Orgrimmar.\n4 Steel Breastplate\n4 Steel Plate Helm","desc":"In the time of legends, Aturk would crush the skulls of his enemies and grind the bone into a fine powder for use in filament. Long gone are those days, ‹race›. The Warchief calls for peace among the clans. Old enemies are now only watched with weary eyes!\nUnbelievable, I know, but such is the will of Thrall.\nEnough lamenting! You are here to learn, and learn you will! Bring me four steel breastplates and four steel helms and you will gain a taste of war!","rew":"You will learn: Orcish War Leggings\nExperience: 3,150","back":"Aturk, like time, waits for no one! Hurry up fool!","done":"It seems you are but another complacent lemming of the Warchief, ‹name›. How disappointing.\nHow I long for a glorious death upon the battlefield. Instead, I am stuck here, by order of Thrall, to teach infants how to craft! Watch and learn, child!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":80.9,"y":23.3,"n":"Aturk the Anvil","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97956":{"id":97956,"t":"Camping 101 fishing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Clyde Kellen in Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your fishing skill to 20","desc":"You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.","back":"I can teach you once you've gained some skill as a fisherman.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Fish Bowl. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":67.2,"y":51,"n":"Clyde Kellen","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94356":{"id":94356,"t":"Craftsmans writ felcloth boots","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Felcloth Boots\nFelcloth Boots","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Felcloth Boots, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Felcloth Boots Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94356","cats":["crafting"]},"94276":{"id":94276,"t":"Craftsmans writ wicked mithril blade","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Wicked Mithril Blade\nWicked Mithril Blade","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Wicked Mithril Blade, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Wicked Mithril Blade Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94276","cats":["crafting"]},"5156":{"id":5156,"t":"Verifying the Corruption","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out and destroy 2 Entropic Beasts and 2 Entropic Horrors while exploring Shatter Scar Vale. After checking to see if the craters there are still filled with corrupt fel water, return to Taronn Redfeather in Felwood.\nEntropic Beast slain : 0/ 2\nEntropic Horror slain : 0/ 2","desc":"To the north, along the east of the road in what's called Shatter Scar Vale, is an area where infernals were called down during the last great war--the craters still scar the land, as do the infernals themselves.\nI am curious about two things. First, are there still entropic elementals roaming the area? And second, are the craters still filled with the corrupt, fetid water that gathered there years ago? Will you help me and check, ‹name›? Be careful though, the infernals destroy anything in their path.","rew":"Money: 1 65 1 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,800","back":"I hope your search goes well, ‹name›. I haven't started heading that far north, but I will admit, the thought of crossing the path of an infernal at any point scares me just a little. The creatures are brainless, but still quite intimidating.","done":"Good that you're alive, ‹name›. Bad that the water still exists. I was hoping to find at least one pure source of water here in Felwood. It looks like my search has failed. The process of healing the land could have been made much easier with its existence.\nI will have to concern myself with saving what forest creatures I can while destroying those that have become so corrupt that they endanger themselves as much as travelers through this once-mighty forest.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":50.9,"y":81.6,"n":"Taronn Redfeather","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4116":{"id":4116,"t":"Corrupted Songflower","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply some Cenarion plant salve to the songflower. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":34.3,"y":52.2,"n":"Corrupted Songflower","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"996":{"id":996,"t":"Corrupted Windblossom","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":57.5,"y":20,"n":"Corrupted Windblossom","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"676":{"id":676,"t":"The Hammer May Fall","lv":32,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Boulderfist Ogres and 10 Boulderfist Enforcers, then find Drum Fel in the Hammerfall outpost in Arathi Highlands.\nBoulderfist Ogre slain : 0/ 8\nBoulderfist Enforcer slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Weaklings... all of them. You, ‹class›, what are you looking at? Think you're something special, huh? Why not prove it?\nThe Hammerfall outpost in Arathi's under attack. Unless we send them help soon, their demise is imminent.\nBut before you go rushing off, you may want to test your skills first. Northeast of Stromgarde in Arathi is an ogre mound inhabited by the Boulderfist tribe. When you can handle the ogres and enforcers there, then report to Drum Fel in Hammerfall.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"I have not the time to sharpen my axe, let alone leave the outpost to slay those beasts that would try and slay my kin.\nYou do not seem to have the experience of a grunt let alone a full-fledged warrior, what do you want, ‹name›?","done":"So, you think you're strong enough to help Hammerfall? So be it.\nTallow either sent you to that ogre mound in the hopes that you would kill yourself or he thinks you're strong enough to aid us. Either way, you're here now and I am in need of more soldiers in our fight against the constant attacks.\nIf you plan on staying in Hammerfall then get some rest, and come speak to me again when you're ready. There's no shortage of fighting to be had.\nHillsbrad Foothills Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.9,"y":19.6,"n":"Tallow","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.2,"y":33.9,"n":"Drum Fel","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"7636":{"id":7636,"t":"Stave of the Ancients","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"You must find and destroy these four demonic corrupters:\nSimone the Seductress.\nKlinfran the Crazed.\nSolenor the Slayer.\nArtorius the Doombringer.\nDestroy these creatures and return to Vartrus the Ancient in Felwood with their heads.\nRefer to the Petrified Bark in your inventory for clues as to their whereabouts.\nYou MUST complete this task by yourself.\nSimone's Head Simone the Seductress\nKlinfran's Head Klinfran the Crazed\nSolenor's Head Solenor the Slayer\nArtorius's Head Artorius the Doombringer\nProvided: Petrified Bark","desc":"Agents of the Burning Legion are still active in our world, ‹class›. These agents corrupt all that they touch. Nature wilts and weeps in their presence.\nYou must track down these demonic corrupters and destroy them, ‹name›. Be warned, you must engage them by yourself or they will flee. As long as you are alone, they will try and destroy you. You must strike at them, turning their arrogance into misery.\nI grant you a piece of my bark, the inscriptions shall lead you to your targets. Retrieve their heads.","rew":"You will receive:\nAncient Rune Etched Stave\nExperience: 9,950","back":"Do not be fooled by their disguises!","done":"You have served us well, ‹name›! Take this stave and combine it with the bow string that Stoma is able to create. Together, they form a most formidable weapon.\nUn'Goro Crater Burning Steppes Silithus Winterspring\nUn'Goro Crater Open the zone on the world map Start Vartrus the Ancient End Vartrus the Ancient Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Hunter Shareable No Quest ID 7636\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 19,900 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] The Ancient Leaf\nFind the owner of the Ancient Petrified Leaf.\nAncient Petrified Leaf\n9,950 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Stave of the Ancients this quest\nYou must find and destroy these four demonic corrupters: Simone the Seductress. Klinfran the Crazed. Solenor the Slayer. Artorius the Doombringer. Destroy these crea\nVartrus the Ancient\n9,950 XP","cats":["hunter"]},"436":{"id":436,"t":"Ironband's Excavation","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Explorer Fellhew.","desc":"Prospector Ironband is heading an excavation of ancient ruins east of the lake. His progress has been slow lately, especially considering all the supplies we've sent him.\nIronband's a stout, honest dwarf who values results, which has me worried that forces are at work against him.\nGo to Ironband's Excavation and speak with Magmar Fellhew. He manages the details of the site and will know why there's a slowdown.\nTo get to the excavation site, go around the southern tip of the lake, then head east.","rew":"Experience: 340\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Jern wants to know what the slowdown is, eh?\nIronband is putting together his latest progress report with details, but I can tell you this:\nIt's the Troggs!!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37.2,"y":47.4,"n":"Jern Hornhelm","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":64.9,"y":66.7,"n":"Magmar Fellhew","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8676":{"id":8676,"t":"Wildmane the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...\nStart Elder Wildmane Zul'Farrak End Elder Wildmane Zul'Farrak Level 60 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 56 58 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 8676","cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1956":{"id":1956,"t":"Power in Uldaman","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve an Obsidian Power Source and bring it to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.\nObsidian Power Source Obsidian Sentinel","desc":"Now that the demon has been removed, we must gain a power source. Unfortunately, the best power sources are usually the oldest and the hardest to get. It's neat how fate likes to take a bite out of you sometimes, isn't it?\nSo you're going to need to go to Uldaman and defeat the obsidian sentinel there. He's big, he's tough, and his power source packs a punch!\nI wish you the best of luck, ‹name›. And if you don't get lucky then, well... it was nice knowing you.","rew":"Experience: 3,900","back":"Have you been to Uldaman, ‹name›? Did you defeat the obsidian sentinel?","done":"You did it? Well done!\nI was chatting with some of my colleagues and when your name came up they said, \"You know that ‹name› sure works well under stress!\"\nBut when I told them I sent you to Uldaman against the obsidian sentinel, they said I was crazy! They said, \"Tabetha, you're crazy! There's no way ‹name› could take on that sentinel!\"\nAnd I said, \"We'll see\", and then they said \"Yeah, we'll see...\"\nWell we sure showed them, didn't we!","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"756":{"id":756,"t":"Thunderhorn Totem","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Stalker Claws and 6 Cougar Claws to Mull Thunderhorn.\n6 Stalker Claws Prairie Stalker 44 %\n6 Cougar Claws Flatland Cougar 44 %","desc":"To create the Thunderhorn Cleansing Totem, you must gather the claws of the predators of the Mulgore plains. Hunt prairie stalkers for their stalker claws and flatland cougars for their cougar claws, then return to me.\nYou will find the prairie stalkers and flatland cougars to the east and west.","rew":"Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"‹name›, do you have the claws I sent you to gather? The Thunderhorn Water Well grows more tainted with each passing hour!","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. The purity with which these beasts hunt is vital in the creation of the next cleansing totem.\nThe goblins will never learn the difference between contending with the land, and living in harmony with it.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.5,"y":63.6,"n":"Mull Thunderhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9236":{"id":9236,"t":"Icebane Breastplate","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -300g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 8 Frozen Runes, 16 Thorium Bars, 2 Arcanite Bars, 4 Essence of Water and 300 gold. You will also need to be of Exalted reputation with the Argent Dawn.\n8 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n16 Thorium Bar\n2 Arcanite Bar\n4 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more\nReach 42000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion (May he rest in peace), I am now able to create an Icebane breastplate. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nIcebane Breastplate","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8276":{"id":8276,"t":"Taking Back Silithus","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.","desc":"Attention, champions of the Horde! There's a threat we've left unchallenged for too long. Tremors in the earth near silithid hives all around Azeroth have alerted us to large movements in their numbers as they prepare for expansion.\nCenarion Circle forces are gathering in Silithus to take the fight to the silithid before it's too late! No more shall they defile our lands!\nAll able-bodied combatants are to report to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold! The silithid shall be vanquished!","rew":"Experience: 2,800\n+10 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Excellent, a new recruit answering the call to arms against the silithid. Welcome to Cenarion Hold, ‹class›. I am pleased to see the words of our emissaries are reaching heroes of your caliber. You will find no shortage of opportunities to help us in our efforts here and I expect you'll quickly prove to be a valuable ally to our cause.\nOrgrimmar Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":47.6,"y":65.8,"n":"Cenarion Emissary Blackhoof","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Windcaller Proudhorn","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"8916":{"id":8916,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Silithus Venom Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Devout Bracers to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\n15 Silithus Venom Sample Stonelash Scorpid 30 % , Stonelash Pincer 30 % , Stonelash Flayer 30 % , Sand Skitterer 30 % and 1 more\nDevout Bracers Crimson Priest 3.7 % , Crimson Initiate 1.9 % , Thuzadin Necromancer 1.6 % in Stratholme , Thuzadin Shadowcaster 1.3 % in Stratholme and 1 more","desc":"Hail, ‹class›! I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world. Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.\nPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.\nI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus. Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.","rew":"You will receive:\nVirtuous Bracers\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you obtained the items I require, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, yes. Mux will be quite happy with this.\nThose bracers were part of a larger armor set. If you're interested in providing me with further assistance, I'd be willing to consider parting with the rest of it.\nOrgrimmar Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"91316":{"id":91316,"t":"Making repairs","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 12 pieces of Sturdy Lumber from Shadowvale in Tirisfal Glades.\n12 Sturdy Lumber","desc":"This far from the Undercity, logistics are challenging and we have a dire shortage of building materials needed to help restore this fortress. I'd like your help with that.\nThe ruined village of Shadowvale can be found in the Whispering Forest, just southwest of here. One of the buildings has an old root cellar used to store all sorts of things. There are likely to be usable materials down there. Scavenge what you can and return to us.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSalvaged Wooden Tower Shield\nMoney: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 875\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"They say location is everything. While this fortress may look imposing perched upon these bluffs, its turning out to be quite the challenge to stay supplied this far from proper civilization. An unfortunate oversight on our part.","done":"I'm glad to see that your trip to Shadowvale bore fruit. I'll send Breton and a few of the other new recruits over later to clear the rest of the cellar out and retrieve anything left down in the dark.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Jorin Croge","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"94436":{"id":94436,"t":"A lesson in divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep.\nShould you misplace your Symbol of Life, return to Danitha Morr for a replacement.\nSpeak with Deathguard Billmuth at Tyr's Watch.","desc":"It's time to demonstrate your ability to channel one of the light's greatest gifts.\nThe item I just gave you is called the Symbol of Life. Take care, as it may cause you some discomfort to handle a talisman of the light such as this. The light may be anathema to the force that created us, but it is still our guide and ally. The pain reminds us of this.\nGo see Deathguard Billmuth downstairs. He just arrived and he has petitioned us for aid. Show him and the Forsaken what a true paladin can do.","done":"So you'll help me, then? Good, good. I'll admit I'm not proud of resorting to... well, resorting to asking paladins for aid. The priests waved me away and you might be my friend's only chance.\nPlease, help me.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.6,"n":"Danitha Morr","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.6,"n":"Deathguard Billmuth","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5636":{"id":5636,"t":"Desperate Prayer","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.","desc":"Elune bless you, good ‹race›. I hope your Light finds you and protects you well this day.\nOne of your priests was here not long ago looking for you. He mentioned you returning to the Hall of Mysteries as soon as possible to speak with High Priest Rohan. It seems you've done well to garner such attention. I wouldn't spend too much time here--your people have need of you.","rew":"You will learn: Desperate Prayer\nExperience: 210","done":"I'm glad you've arrived, ‹name›. There are many things we will have to discuss, but more importantly is your training in the ways of the Light.\nThere are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we'll begin discussing some of those now.\nTeldrassil Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.6,"y":56.7,"n":"Laurna Morninglight","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":44.6,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"3636":{"id":3636,"t":"Bring the Light","lv":42,"min":39,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Archbishop Bendictus wants you to slay Amnennar the Coldbringer in Razorfen Downs.\nAmnennar the Coldbringer slain in Razorfen Downs","desc":"The Scourge is a persistent threat to the Alliance, a fact I am sure you know quite well. Recently, we have come across some very peculiar findings, ‹name›.\nIn the Barrens lies a horrid tangle of briars called Razorfen Downs. While once it was the home of simple quilboar, now it has become apparent that a pact was made with the Scourge, creating creatures far worse... They are now ruled by the lich, Amnennar the Coldbringer.\nAlign yourself with the Light, ‹name›; put an end to this evil union.","rew":"You will receive:\nVanquisher's Sword Amberglow Talisman\nExperience: 4,300\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Amnennar must be eradicated. Go, swiftly.","done":"Thank you , ‹name›. The Scourge will now think twice before attempting to bolster its ranks again.\nMay you be blessed by the Light.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.3,"y":45.5,"n":"Archbishop Benedictus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["razorfen-downs"]},"116":{"id":116,"t":"Dry Times","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Barkeep Daniels of Lakeshire needs a keg of Thunderbrew Lager, a cask of Merlot, a bottle of Moonshine and a skin of Sweet Rum.\nKeg of Thunderbrew\nCask of Merlot sold by Roberto Pupellyverbos\nBottle of Moonshine sold by Barkeep Hann\nSkin of Sweet Rum sold by Barkeep Dobbins","desc":"I find myself in quite a pinch here, ‹name›. The bottles are close to running dry. The latest booze shipment is long overdue. The orc invasion has been hell.\nPerhaps you can go to work for me?\nI need you to pick up a keg of Thunderbrew Lager from Grimbooze Thunderbrew in the Westfall hills, a cask of Merlot from Stormwind, a bottle of Moonshine from Darkshire and a skin of Sweet Rum from Goldshire. Bring those back to me and I will see to it you are rewarded.","rew":"You will receive:\nFinely Woven Cloak A Bulging Coin Purse\nExperience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I need you to pick up a keg of Thunderbrew Lager from Grimbooze Thunderbrew in the Westfall hills, a cask of Merlot from Stormwind, a bottle of Moonshine from Darkshire and a skin of Sweet Rum from Goldshire. Bring those back to me and I will see to it you are rewarded.","done":"A job well done, ‹name›! I know well the roads you had to journey to procure this fine array of liquor. But my patrons will be happy once again!\nMy wife is quite a seamstress. Please accept this cloak she made in return for your services.\nRedridge Mountains Duskwood Elwynn Forest Stormwind City Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":21.4,"y":44,"n":"Barkeep Daniels","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8836":{"id":8836,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with Darnassus.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.2,"y":38.7,"n":"Officer Lunalight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"78676":{"id":78676,"t":"The eye of bhossca","lv":35,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Reported by players.","obj":"Find The Eye of Bhossca inside of the Scarlet Monastery. Then, return it to C's dead drop near Pyrewood Village. You must complete the job alone.\nEye of Bhossca","desc":"<A note sits in the chest>\nGlad to have you back, ‹name›.\nThe latest object of my desire is an artifact known as the Eye of Bhossca. My sources tell me the eye is somewhere within the Scarlet Monastery. As with Shadowfang Keep, you must infiltrate the monastery alone.\nIt may behoove you to find a disguise before going in. It will make getting around a touch easier. I'm sure you could find something on the monastery's grounds.\nReturn the eye here, and payment will be delivered as before.\n- C","rew":"You will receive:\nRuby-Adorned Blade\nExperience: 3,450","back":"<The chest sits, empty.>","done":"<You place The Eye of Bhossca into the chest>","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":47.1,"y":71.1,"n":"Dead Drop","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"8356":{"id":8356,"t":"Flexing for Nougat","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Do a flex emote at Innkeeper Allison, and in exchange you'll receive Stormwind Nougat!","desc":"That's an... interesting costume you have on. Even though you're being nice and helping a sick child trick-or-treat this year, I'm afraid I'm going to have to ask you perform a trick for me!\nLet's see... you look so strong and buff in that... costume... let's see you flex! Yes, go on now and flex for me, strong man/woman!\nWhen and only when you flex, I'll give you some tasty Stormwind Nougat. It's a great Hallow's End treat.","rew":"You will receive:\nStormwind Nougat","back":"No candy until you flex for me, ‹name›...","done":"You are truly mighty, haha! Well done, and thanks for being such a good sport. Here's your candy.\nHappy Hallow's End, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":60.4,"y":75.3,"n":"Innkeeper Allison","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"516":{"id":516,"t":"Beren's Peril","lv":21,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate Beren's Peril, then kill 6 Ravenclaw Drudgers and 6 Ravenclaw Guardians, then return to Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.\nRavenclaw Drudger slain : 0/ 6\nRavenclaw Guardian slain : 0/ 6","desc":"I have received reports that a group of undead are holing up to prepare for an attack against us. Armed with this information, we can turn the tables and attack them first, nipping their little plan in the bud.\nUnfortunately, my information is spotty, at best. They are reported to be hiding in a location known as Beren's Peril. The exact location is unknown, but it appears to be a cave in the hills, near a pocket of Dalaran wizards.\nI trust your resourcefulness. Find them, and put them down.","rew":"You will receive:\nWand of Decay\nExperience: 1,250\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you located their base yet, ‹name›? Time is of the essence!","done":"If our scouts and agents continue to procure valuable information such as this, we shall have the Lich King's Scourge removed from our lands in no time.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44,"y":40.9,"n":"Shadow Priest Allister","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"81956":{"id":81956,"t":"Conjurers codex","lv":45,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Conjurer's Codex","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 390","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nConjurer's Codex (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1076":{"id":1076,"t":"Devils in Westfall","lv":21,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Dust Devil Debris to Collin Mauren in Stormwind.\nDust Devil Debris Dust Devil","desc":"Ah, I think I have it. A messaging spell... I believe that's the effect he's looking for.\nI'll have to create a scroll with the spell impressed upon it. To do that I'll need debris from a dust devil.\nWhile I gather the rest of the components, why don't you head to Westfall and find one of the foul creatures? They are dangerous, but I'm sure it's nothing you can't handle if you're willing to subject yourself to one of Gaxim's experiments.\nI'll be here when you return.","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Have you found the component I need?","done":"Allow me just a few moments and I shall have your scroll ready for you.\nStormwind City Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":53,"y":86.6,"n":"Collin Mauren","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"7796":{"id":7796,"t":"Additional Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","back":"Greetings once again, ‹name›! Our need for runecloth is constant, and we can always use additional resources if you are willing to part with them. For an additional stack of twenty runecloth, I will make sure that you are recognized for your continuing efforts on behalf of Stormwind.\nWhenever you are ready to hand in the stack of runecloth, I'll accept it.","done":"‹name› - without heroes like you working on behalf of Stormwind, we'd surely suffer. Thank you for your continued efforts!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":53.9,"y":81.7,"n":"Clavicus Knavingham","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"596":{"id":596,"t":"Bloody Bone Necklaces","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 25 Bloody Bone Necklaces to Kin'weelay at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\n25 Bloody Bone Necklace Bloodscalp Scavenger 17 % , Bloodscalp Mystic 17 % , Bloodscalp Beastmaster 17 % , Bloodscalp Shaman 17 % and 4 more","desc":"I was sent to Grom'gol to aid Nimboya on his quest, but... I too have reasons for being here.\nThe Bloodscalp tribe is enemy to our tribe. Collecting trophies of our enemies gives us power over them. You may aid our tribe by hunting our enemies.\nThey dwell to the north. Slay Bloodscalp trolls and take from them their bloody bone necklaces. Collect many, and your reward will be great.","rew":"You will receive:\nBloodbone Band\nExperience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"The Bloodscalps will one day be crushed by the Darkspears! Do you have the necklaces of our doomed foe?","done":"Ah, very good. I will boil these, and leech them, and the spirits of their owners will weaken as I render their necklaces to paste!\nHere, ‹name›. This will repay my debt to you.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.3,"y":27.7,"n":"Kin'weelay","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"196":{"id":196,"t":"Raptor Mastery","lv":41,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hemet Nesingwary wants you to kill 10 Jungle Stalkers.\nJungle Stalker slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Let's see how you handle this next challenge. There is a cagey breed of raptor out there. We call them Jungle Stalkers. They are far more difficult to track down and kill than the other breeds you've been trying your luck at. Kill 10 Jungle Stalkers and I'll tip you off to the best hunting yet.","rew":"Experience: 2,450","back":"Bah! What are you doing standing around, ‹name›! A true big game hunter never gives up once his prey is in his sights. Those Jungle Stalkers aren't going to come running up to this campfire and throw themselves in it. Silly bloke.","done":"Ho ho!! We have ourselves a true raptor slayer! Nicely done, old chap!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.8,"n":"Hemet Nesingwary","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8196":{"id":8196,"t":"Essence Mangoes","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Zandalar Honor Token\nReach 9000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Essence Mango","back":"The extremely potent essence mango grows across many of the islands in the South Seas. A single mango will refresh those who eat it, both physically and mentally. If you've never had one, you do yourself a disservice!\nWe have enough of a supply here on the isle to offer you a handful in exchange for a Zandalar Honor Token. Speak with Vinchaxa if you need to learn how to get tokens; otherwise, let's get to the business at hand!","done":"A fair trade, my friend - please enjoy the luscious fruits of the South Seas, with the tribe's blessing.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.1,"y":16,"n":"Rin'wosho the Trader","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1396":{"id":1396,"t":"Encroaching Wildlife","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Young Sawtooth Crocolisks, 10 Sorrow Spinners and 10 Swamp Jaguars then return to Watcher Biggs in the Swamp of Sorrows.\nYoung Sawtooth Crocolisk slain : 0/ 8\nSorrow Spinner slain : 0/ 10\nSwamp Jaguar slain : 0/ 10","desc":"My caravan was destined for the eastern coast, but we did not reach our goal. Lost Ones attacked us, killing guards and dashing supplies.\nI alone survived their assault. I have sworn to protect what supplies remain, but wild creatures skulk near. Please, help me defend my camp from the beasts!","rew":"Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"The swamp creatures press close, ‹name›. Please, you must defend the camp!","done":"The sounds of animals are now faint, more distant. Thank you, ‹name›. Now let's hope they don't return!","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":26.7,"y":59.8,"n":"Watcher Biggs","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"8756":{"id":8756,"t":"The Qiraji Conqueror","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 9,950\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Never have I seen such tenacity! The Bronze Flight grants you one final enchantment. The Timeless One himself has requested it so!\nHand me your signet ring so that I may make the necessary adjustments.","done":"Rise, Qiraji Conqueror! Rise and be recognized!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"916":{"id":916,"t":"Webwood Venom","lv":4,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Webwood Venom Sacs to Gilshalan Windwalker at Aldrassil.\n10 Webwood Venom Sac Webwood Spider 80 %","desc":"I came to Shadowglen to observe the webwood spiders that dwell in the Shadowthread Cave. They are cousin to a much smaller variety of spider; I believe the world tree has had a profound effect on them, and I would like specimens to study to confirm this.\nFirst, I would like some of their venom. Gather Webwood venom sacs from the spiders in and around the Shadowthread Cave, to the north. I can then examine them for similarities with their smaller cousin's venom.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nThistlewood Maul Thistlewood Dagger Thistlewood Staff Thistlewood Blade\nExperience: 360\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Did you gather the venom sacs, ‹name›?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. When I return to Darnassus I will compare the venom within these sacs with the venom of other spiders. It is my belief that it will have properties linked to the recent growth of our new world tree.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.8,"y":41.7,"n":"Gilshalan Windwalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"97236":{"id":97236,"t":"Fang of githyiss","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the Fang of Githyiss to someone interested in the study of spiders in Aldrassil.","desc":"A fresh specimen from a beast of this size is quite a find. Perhaps someone in Aldrassil familiar with the study of spiders would be interested in the fang.","rew":"Money: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 450\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","done":"My, my. How I do love surprises, ‹name›.\nThis specimen will surely help further my studies.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.8,"y":41.6,"n":"Gilshalan Windwalker","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"836":{"id":836,"t":"Rescue OOX-09/HL!","lv":48,"min":43,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort OOX-09/HL to the shoreline beyond Overlook Cliff, then report to Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay.","desc":"The gnome's voice crackles once again from the robot:\n\"I need to move OOX-09/HL to an open, safe place so it can begin a lengthy take-off procedure. It has built-in cloaking, but I need time on my end to make it operational again. Escort the robot from its current location to, let's say, the shoreline beyond Overlook Cliff! That should be a perfect place, and long enough, to get things online!\"\n\"Escort it safely to the shore, and then come talk to me in Booty Bay! Oglethorpe Obnoticus - out!\"","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGnomish Inventor Boots Gnomish Water Sinking Device\nExperience: 5,450\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","done":"Oh, YOU'RE the great savior of OOX-09/HL! I cannot even begin to express my thanks for your assistance! My homing robot series needs more development, but your recovery has saved me countless hours of extra rebuilding time, as well as many gold pieces in manufacture costs!\nPlease, take your choice of any of these items I have. Thank you again for your generous assistance ‹name›, my robots and I are in your debt!\nThe Hinterlands Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":49.4,"y":37.7,"n":"Homing Robot OOX-09/HL","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.4,"y":76.4,"n":"Oglethorpe Obnoticus","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"356":{"id":356,"t":"Rear Guard Patrol","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Bleeding Horrors and 8 Wandering Spirits, then report back to Linnea at her camp.\nBleeding Horror slain : 0/ 8\nWandering Spirit slain : 0/ 8","desc":"The defenders on The Bulwark protecting Tirisfal from the Plaguelands are on constant alert. But sometimes Scourge will slip past them.\nOur success at the Bulwark depends on a one-front battle - we cannot allow an attack from the rear, nor can we allow our defenders' supply line to be cut.\nAssist the Bulwark. Patrol east and slay any Scourge you find. Spend particular effort at the Balnir Farmstead to the east. It has become a haven for interloping Scourge.","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do you have a report of your patrol?","done":"Very good. Your efforts do much to keep the Scourge at bay. A commendation will be sent to my superior, Executor Zygand.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.5,"y":60.3,"n":"Deathguard Linnea","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"99156":{"id":99156,"t":"Rear guard patrol","lv":13,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Riptear's Heart to Deathguard Linnea.\nRiptear's Heart","desc":"Damn it all! A new report came in while you were on patrol. There has been a sighting of a rogue abomination wandering Eastern Tirisfal Glades, near Venomweb Vale.\nSomething is wrong. Abominations don't just slip through the Bulwark unnoticed.\nKeep this matter on a strictly need-to-know basis. That said, such a creature will not fall easily; you will need allies if you wish to be more than its next meal.\nSee this through, and you will be duly rewarded. Bring me its heart as proof of the deed.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRiptear's Cleaver Riptear's Spare Arm Thrice-Stitched Flesh\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you dealt with our little problem?","done":"You are a testament to the cunning and coordination that all Forsaken possess--something the mindless Scourge will never have.\nPlease accept this as thanks for your efforts, as promised.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.4,"y":60.2,"n":"Deathguard Linnea","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"1716":{"id":1716,"t":"Devourer of Souls","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Takar the Seer in the Barrens.","desc":"A succubus is a devourer of souls, destroyer of hearts, and dominator of minds. It knows nothing but evil.\nThis will be the creature you will learn to summon and control, but it cannot be brought into our world without a stimulus.\nWith a symbol of love as bait, it will surely answer your call. Then you can defeat it, and make it your tool.\nIt will be hard to find something of this nature, though. You should speak with Takar the Seer. You will find him in the Barrens of Kalimdor near Camp Taurajo.","rew":"Experience: 775","done":"Was your crossing difficult, ‹name›? You have come a long way to speak with me. But fear not, I know why Gakin has sent you, and he was wise to, for I can help you in your search.\nStormwind City The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85.2,"n":"Gakin the Darkbinder","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":49.3,"y":57.1,"n":"Takar the Seer","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1476":{"id":1476,"t":"Hearts of the Pure","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the hearts of Dalin Forgewright and Corma Villard to Carendin Halgar in the Temple of the Damned.\nDalin's Heart\nCorma's Heart","desc":"Coaxing a succubus will require the hearts of the pure. But is any mortal without vice?\nThrough bits of overheard stories, I found two humans that should do.\nThe first is Dalin Forgewright, who has dedicated himself to the care of the Lordaeron refuges, whom are refused by their kin at the Greymane Wall.\nThe other is Corma Villard, a woman who remains faithful to her lost love, wandering the Wetlands for a sign of her.\nDeliver their hearts to Carendin. But first, let me show you your quarry.","rew":"Experience: 1,550","back":"I have been pleasantly surprised by the speed of your progress so far, ‹name›. Bring me the hearts and you will impress me once again.","done":"The heart of a goodly man seems much the same as any, when you see it like this, don't you think?\nPerhaps we possess something of a... different... view on the subject. These will do, though. I have no doubt that a succubus would be attracted by their purity.\nUndercity Silverpine Forest Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":84.8,"y":14.8,"n":"Godrick Farsan","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":26,"n":"Carendin Halgar","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"2996":{"id":2996,"t":"Seeking Strahad","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.","desc":"I have taught you skills in the past, but the time has come for another to teach you. He is in Ratchet, and his name is Strahad. He is human, but do not let that fool you into thinking he is weak. He is powerful even though he may be small. He can teach you about more powerful summonings--I feel you are ready. Go to him now. He is in Ratchet... above the port town next to his tower.","rew":"Experience: 600","done":"A busy day in Ratchet, isn't it? How I enjoy watching the toil of a port city. So much mystery, so much adventure... so much ignorance.\nIs that hatred I see in your eyes, ‹name›? Good, we will put that to good use.\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":45.3,"n":"Gan'rul Bloodeye","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1796":{"id":1796,"t":"Components for the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe","lv":31,"min":31,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Robes of the Arcana to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.\nRobes of Arcana","desc":"The first item I will aid you in creating is a robe. You will gather the items for me, and we will put them together. Afterwards, assuming you succeed, you will have the first of many items that will make you more powerful and aid you in your struggles.\nTo start, you must have crafted Robes of Arcana. A tailor can make this for you, or perhaps you can purchase one from someone else--I'd be most impressed if you could make it yourself--but regardless, bring me the robes, and we shall go from there.","rew":"Experience: 2,500","back":"How goes your search for the robes, ‹name›? Have you created them yourself? Such personal touches I find make the imbuing of magic that much sweeter. It gives you a greater sense of accomplishment. But I understand if you choose the quicker path and have it made for you - there's something to be said for such... ambition.","done":"This will do nicely, ‹name›.\nAll magical items must begin with an item of high quality. The more effort and skill put into an item, the greater the magics it can hold. Rare and more expensive components hold the magic better. You will not regret having the robes fashioned into the ones we will make for you later on.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7876":{"id":7876,"t":"Quell the Silverwing Usurpers","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,650 experience instead of 8,150, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Enter Warsong Gulch and defeat the Alliance, gain a Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor, and bring it to Captain Shatterskull at the Mor'shan Base Camp.\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The wilds of the Ashenvale forest will succumb to the might of the Horde, ‹race›. Nothing the Silverwing say or do can stop our sovereign imperative. Kalimdor belongs to the Horde. How dare they attempt to prevent us from harvesting what is rightfully ours!\nLet the pride swell in your chest as you cut down their weak attempts at slowing our progress. Destroy the Silverwing Sentinels, and earn a Warsong mark of honor. Return to me with such a mark, ‹name›, and you will be rewarded.","rew":"Money: 2 50 2 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The blood of our enemies is a mark of honor. Do you have such a mark?","done":"<Captain Shatterskull roars in triumph.>\nHow much more can they withstand? How many more Alliance filth must perish at the hands of the Horde for them to retreat? Only time will tell, ‹race›.\nLevel 55 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 51 53 58 Side Orc, Undead, Tauren, Troll Type PvP Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7876","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5236":{"id":5236,"t":"Return to the Bulwark","lv":58,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Filled Gahrron's Withering Bottle to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\nFilled Gahrron's Withering Bottle\nProvided: Filled Gahrron's Withering Bottle","desc":"You carefully close the spigot in the control panel, watching the cauldron's putrid ichors drip into the empty bottle.\nWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark to complete the mission.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,100\n+50 reputation with Undercity\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Gahrron's Withering houses the last cauldron that we need to acquire access to here in the west. Once we have a sample of the plague from that cauldron, we will be able to introduce our reagents into the environment through four separate vessels! The Scourge will be hard pressed to keep us out of all four, even with the power of Kel'Thuzad behind them.","done":"Congratulations ‹name›, you've unlocked the last cauldron for us! Apothecary Dithers will soon know what this cauldron requires as far as reagents needed for the mix.\nAs for you, I am sure that High Executor Derrington will want to thank you personally for the assistance you've given us. Without you, our struggle against the Scourge would have been nearly insurmountable. I thank you, mighty ‹class›.\nWestern Plaguelands Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":62.5,"y":58.5,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83,"y":71.9,"n":"Shadow Priestess Vandis","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"36":{"id":36,"t":"Westfall Stew","lv":10,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Verna Furlbrow wants you to deliver her recipe for Westfall Stew to Salma Saldean.\nVerna's Westfall Stew Recipe\nProvided: Verna's Westfall Stew Recipe","desc":"I never thought the day would come when I'd leave the farm. But the fields are overrun with thieves and it's far too dangerous for us here now. As soon as Farmer Furlbrow gets the wagon fixed, we'll be on our way.\nMaybe you could do me a favor? Let me scribble down my recipe for Westfall stew. Please take it to Salma Saldean over on the farm yonder. The Saldean's farm is just beyond the fork in the road.","rew":"Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I'm going to miss that Verna Furlbrow so much. I don't suppose you happened to see her on your way here?","done":"That Verna was always such a sweet lass. We'll miss her here in Westfall but between you and me, she's a city girl at heart and Stormwind will suit her just fine. But enough gossip! Now we can make Westfall Stew!","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":59.9,"y":19.4,"n":"Verna Furlbrow","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":56.4,"y":30.5,"n":"Salma Saldean","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"276":{"id":276,"t":"Tramping Paws","lv":21,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 15 Mosshide Gnolls and 10 Mosshide Mongrels, then return to Rethiel the Greenwarden in the Wetlands.\nMosshide Gnoll slain : 0/ 15\nMosshide Mongrel slain : 0/ 10","desc":"The Mosshide Gnolls have lived in the Wetlands peacefully for many years, but now grow in numbers. Their feet stamp flat the fen's bushes and flowers, and their foul axes cut too much wood to fuel their fires.\nThey are no longer in balance with the land. For the Wetlands to survive, the Gnolls must be reduced.\nKill 15 Mosshide Gnolls and 10 Mosshide Mongrels. Hunt them to the south, near the Dwarven gate of Algaz. After you do this, return to me.","rew":"Experience: 1,250","back":"Your task is still at hand, young ‹class›.","done":"By reducing the Gnolls' number, you have tended to the health of the Wetlands. Although my faith in your people has been taxed in the past, ‹race›, it may yet be restored.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":56.4,"y":40.4,"n":"Rethiel the Greenwarden","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"88756":{"id":88756,"t":"Bring back a bang","lv":32,"min":27,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Retrieve 3 Stolen Explosives from the Dark Iron Dwarf camps.\n3 Stolen Explosives","desc":"The Dark Irons have a few camps east of here on Direforge Hill, and they've stolen a bunch of explosives from our construction site and hauled 'em back to their tents.\nI don't need tae tell ya what kinda mischief Dark Irons can get up tae with a barrel o' powder!\nI know the Dark Irons are dangerous, but we need those barrels back. You can tell 'em from other barrels because of the red markings on 'em. We cannae let the Dark Irons keep 'em!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Ez-Thro Dynamite\nMoney: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":50,"y":18.2,"n":"Ashlan Stonesmirk","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92596":{"id":92596,"t":"The high order","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Have a seat and speak with Rathiril Sunlance.\nListen to Rathiril Sunlance","desc":"The aura of arcane energy that surrounds you is strong, even though you are not initiated as a mage. I am quite sure that you are going to be a capable adventurer, and your connection with our ancient magic will only ever be a boon to you even if you were to never utter a single word of power in spellcasting.\nCome, let us sit and speak some on my order, the nature of the arcane here on Zephras, and the plight of our people.","back":"Our land is going through changes, but there may yet be some good to come of this.","done":"The High Order's mission is vital to the survival of our people. We hold our elemental benefactors in the utmost regard, but we must face reality; they are gone now, and we are on our own.\nBetween threats from within such as the Al'Aketh, and uncertainties of our security on this plane, it is our destiny as Highborne descendants of our ancestral home of Eldre'Thalas to use our gifts to ensure that the shen'dorei can stand on our own once again.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45,"y":46.4,"n":"Rathiril Sunlance","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92516":{"id":92516,"t":"Hippogryph harrassment","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 8 Hippogryph Youths, 6 Hippogryph Protectors and a Hippogryph Matriarch in the Shen'dar Highlands.\nHippogryph Youth slain : 0/ 8\nHippogryph Protector slain : 0/ 6\nHippogryph Matriarch slain","desc":"A flock of Hippogryph have recently established nesting grounds southeast of Shen'dar Village and they've been wreaking havoc on travelers on the road. I need someone to head down there and thin them out for us.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","done":"Well done, and quickly too. Not too bad at all.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":44.4,"y":45,"n":"Teeri Wellwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8116":{"id":8116,"t":"Vision of Voodress","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","rew":"You will receive:\nVision of Voodress\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"NULL","done":"You and Maywiki have something in common, mon. We both be ‹class›! Although, Maywiki is more of a mystic and you be more of a scrub. Still, we both know what the great spirits bring.\nAs a gift I give to you this orb to wear around your neck. Look deep inside and see the village of Voodress in the South Seas! Let it lift your spirits!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});